        "original_id": "d1ff498f-1c87-5f5a-ba89-9cb86e9faf7c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Projects: One Manhattan Square, Time Warner Center, 247 Cherry\n- Companies: Extell Development Company, The Related Companies, AREA Property Partners, Apollo Real Estate Advisors, Skidmore, Owings & Merrill\n- People: David Childs, Mustafa Kemal Abadan\n- Places: Two Bridges, Manhattan, New York City\n\nFacts:\n- One Manhattan Square, also known as 227 Cherry Street or 250 South Street, is a residential skyscraper project in Two Bridges, Manhattan, New York City.\n- Extell Development Company is developing One Manhattan Square.\n- One Manhattan Square is planned to stand 80 stories or 850 feet (259 m) tall and may include a new supermarket in its base.\n- 247 Cherry will be adjacent to One Manhattan Square.\n- Time Warner Center was developed by The Related Companies and AREA Property Partners, which was formerly known as Apollo Real Estate Advisors.\n- Time Warner Center was designed by David Childs and Mustafa Kemal Abadan of Skidmore, Owings & Merrill.\n- Time Warner Center consists of two 750-foot twin towers connected by a multistory atrium containing upscale retail shops.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
